On Jul 11, 9:48 pm, Doug Freyburger <dfrey...@yahoo.com> wrote:
> "Blog the Haggis" <NoS...@NoSpam.org> wrote:
> > I currently have a priest game where I have both a +7
> > Mjollnir and a +7 Grayswandir and I was wondering which one
> > I should use?

> Grayswandir wins against other artifact weapons most of the
> time.  At +0 Mojo tends to beat Gray but but the time you
> get either to +7 the doubling of Gray more than makes up
> for the shock damage.

> > From the spoilers it looks like Grayswandir does more damage
> > at Expert level than Mjollnir but I'm restricted to Basic in
> > saber. So the question is does Grayswandir at Basic do more
> > damage than Mjollnir at Expert proficiency?

> Expert is vastly overrated for melee weapons.  It is for throwing
> missiles and casting spells.  Basic is fine.

Yes and no.  Expert or skilled increase the probability of
hitting, when you don't have much experience.  I find that it's
often possible to get to skilled when your experience is still
low enough to make it worth while.  Expert less so, although if
you're playing a fighter type, like Valk or Samurai, and don't
have a robe, you might as well; even at expert, spell casting
isn't going to work reliably, so once you've got your ranged
weapon to expert, there's nothing else to use the slots for.
(For a Priest, however, I agree.  Leave it at Basic.)

